\[\phi=\tan^{-1}\!\left(\frac{p_{y}}{p_{x}}\right). \tag{1.4}\]

(where \(p_{x}\), \(p_{y}\), \(p_{z}\) are the components of the momentum \(p\), with \(p_{z}\) being along the beam direction). The rapidity is defined by the equation:

\[y=\frac{1}{2}\ln\!\left(\frac{E+p_{z}}{E-p_{z}}\right). \tag{1.5}\]

